    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3cb699d7-198b-5d7e-8824-21bc4ce81ab9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=5xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we define $f(x,y)=5xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement \u201cAt every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\u201d is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement \u201cAt every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\u201d is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement \u201cAt every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\u201d is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.",
